@startuml f8-task-finalization
title F8 — Task finalization (no queues) + EX frees one slot

|AG|
start
:Agent loop complete;
:Emit final result
 with stdout and exit code;

|EX|
:Capture final stdout and exit code;
:REST POST /events
 to Event Router
 with status=terminal, payload=result;

|ER|
:Persist final event in ER DB;
:UPDATE task status to terminal in ER DB;
:Push to subscribers (API Gateway);
:Send webhook to Automation (if configured);
:slots_in_use = slots_in_use minus 1;

note right
  Each completed task destroys ONE
  container and frees ONE slot on the EX,
  not the entire capacity. If the EX had
  capacity N and was running N containers,
  all N must complete before slots_in_use
  returns to 0. This single completion event
  frees exactly one slot.
end note

if (slots_in_use less than capacity?) then (yes, EX still has free slots)
  :EX is still busy with other tasks,
   but has at least one free slot;
else (no, EX is fully idle)
  :EX has no running tasks;
endif

fork
  |API Gateway|
  :Receive final event from ER;
  :Proxy to UI over WS (per F3);
  -->[ws] "Operator sees terminal status"

  |Operator|
  :Receive WS final frame;

  |EX|
  :Stop container
   with SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after grace;
  :Unmount tmpfs (plaintext gone);

fork again
  |EX|
  :REST POST /executors/:id/ready
   signal available for next task;

  |ER|
  :Receive ready signal;
  :ER can now match a new pending task
   to this EX if slots_in_use is less than capacity
   (see F4);

fork again
  |ER|
  :Invalidate scope_token cache entry
   in ER DB;
end fork

stop

@enduml